James inquired about loading data in RShiny upon selecting an item from a picker and dynamically plotting it based on a slider adjustment. I guided him to use `observeEvent` for response to picker selection, `reactiveValues` to store the loaded data for later access, and `renderPlotly` for dynamic plotting. I provided a sample Shiny app structure, outlining the UI components, data loading logic, and plotting process. Key points included ensuring the data is reactive with `reactiveValues`, triggering data loading on picker changes with `observeEvent`, and confirming data availability in plots with `req`. This guidance aimed to help James implement his desired features efficiently in RShiny.
